  "accepted_answer": {
    "post_number": 2,
    "username": "sayan",
    "name": null,
    "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discourse.onlinedegree.iitm.ac.in/sayan/{size}/112713_2.png",
    "excerpt": "<p>You can run all basic commands on Terminal. Yes the terminal reflects your system’s state, it is not some virtual machine running inside your mac. Deleting files will delete them from your mac. We expect you to know what a command does before executing it.</p>\n<p>Additionally you can simply create a folder where you test the commands out while starting out and avoid leaving that folder, so it is less likely you will delete unrelated files.</p>\n<p>You do not need to install ubuntu.</p>",
    "accepter_name": null,
    "accepter_username": "21f3000759"
  },
